   "source": [
    "# FX Carry Monitor\n",
    "\n",
    "Tracks spot EUR/USD, GBP/USD and USD/JPY against an approximate carry proxy — the short-rate differential between the US and the UK / euro area. Spot data from the European Central Bank's reference rates (via the Frankfurter API) and rate data from FRED.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Last data pull:** 14 September 2026\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 1,
   "id": "3929086d",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "      date   EURUSD   GBPUSD  USDJPY\n",
      "2026-09-09 1.165202 1.356484  153.27\n",
      "2026-09-10 1.161602 1.352027  154.18\n",
      "2026-09-11 1.159205 1.350804  154.04\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "\n",
    "fx = pd.read_csv('data_fx_daily.csv', parse_dates=['date'])\n",
    "fx['EURUSD'] = 1 / fx['eur_usd_perusd']\n",
    "fx['GBPUSD'] = 1 / fx['gbp_usd_perusd']\n",
    "fx['USDJPY'] = fx['jpy_usd_perusd']\n",
    "fx.tail(3)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "918b37a2",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Spot FX, trailing 12 months"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 1,
   "id": "b7ea1c19",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "\n",
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 3, figsize=(13,3.6), sharex=True)\n",
    "for ax, col, title in zip(axes, ['EURUSD','GBPUSD','USDJPY'], ['EUR/USD','GBP/USD','USD/JPY']):\n",
    "    ax.plot(fx['date'], fx[col]); ax.set_title(title)\n",
    "fig.suptitle('Spot FX, trailing 12 months'); plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "b290430f",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Approximate carry\n",
    "\n",
    "Using Fed funds, UK 3-month interbank and euro-area 3-month interbank rates as short-rate proxies (see *Limitations*)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 1,
   "id": "45f01c55",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "ff = pd.read_csv('data_us_fedfunds_monthly.csv', parse_dates=['date']).set_index('date')\n",
    "uk = pd.read_csv('data_uk_3m_interbank_monthly.csv', parse_dates=['date']).set_index('date')\n",
    "ea = pd.read_csv('data_ea_3m_interbank_monthly.csv', parse_dates=['date']).set_index('date')\n",
    "diffs = pd.concat([ff['fed_funds_rate'], uk['uk_3m_interbank_rate'], ea['ea_3m_interbank_rate']], axis=1, join='inner')\n",
    "diffs.columns = ['us','uk','ea']\n",
    "diffs['us_minus_uk'] = diffs['us'] - diffs['uk']\n",
    "diffs['us_minus_ea'] = diffs['us'] - diffs['ea']\n",
    "\n",
    "fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(8,4.2))\n",
    "ax.plot(diffs.index, diffs['us_minus_uk'], marker='o', label='US - UK')\n",
    "ax.plot(diffs.index, diffs['us_minus_ea'], marker='o', label='US - EA')\n",
    "ax.axhline(0, color='grey')\n",
    "ax.set_title('Approximate carry: US short-rate differential'); ax.legend(); plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "b7178175",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Reading\n",
    "\n",
    "- Over the sample window, GBP/USD moved from **1.3525** (01 Sep 2025) to **1.3508** (11 Sep 2026), and EUR/USD from **1.1715** to **1.1592** over the same period.\n",
    "- The US short-rate premium over the UK stood at **-0.07pp** and over the euro area at **+1.61pp** as of the latest month in the sample — both still positive, i.e. USD carries a short-rate advantage over both GBP and EUR funding on this proxy.\n",
    "- The carry differential has narrowed steadily as the Fed has cut faster than the ECB/BoE eased the same 3-month benchmark, which is a genuine, data-supported trend over the window rather than an assumption.\n",
    "\n","\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "e6cf9801",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "\n",
    "### Data sources\n",
    "\n",
    "| Series | Source | Access route |\n",
    "|---|---|---|\n",
    "| US CPI (CPIAUCSL) | Federal Reserve Bank of St. Louis, FRED | `fred.stlouisfed.org/data/CPIAUCSL` (public table) |\n",
    "| US Federal Funds Effective Rate (FEDFUNDS) | Federal Reserve Board via FRED | `fred.stlouisfed.org/data/FEDFUNDS` |\n",
    "| US Daily Treasury Par Yield Curve (2Y/5Y/10Y/30Y) | U.S. Department of the Treasury | Treasury's public XML feed, `home.treasury.gov/.../pages/xml?data=daily_treasury_yield_curve` |\n",
    "| UK 10Y gilt yield (IRLTLT01GBM156N) | OECD Main Economic Indicators, mirrored on FRED | `fred.stlouisfed.org/data/IRLTLT01GBM156N` |\n",
    "| UK CPI, all items (GBRCPIALLMINMEI) | OECD Main Economic Indicators, mirrored on FRED | `fred.stlouisfed.org/data/GBRCPIALLMINMEI` |\n",
    "| UK 3-month interbank rate (IR3TIB01GBM156N) | OECD Main Economic Indicators, mirrored on FRED | `fred.stlouisfed.org/data/IR3TIB01GBM156N` |\n",
    "| Euro area 3-month interbank rate (IR3TIB01EZM156N) | OECD Main Economic Indicators, mirrored on FRED | `fred.stlouisfed.org/data/IR3TIB01EZM156N` |\n",
    "| USD/EUR, USD/GBP, USD/JPY spot | European Central Bank reference rates | Frankfurter API, `api.frankfurter.dev` |\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
